# px60: compiler for the dev image; kernel/wolf.pin is the build-host compiler.
# px65 (R-px65-2): v0.2.35 carries the musl portability fix (wolf-lang#886,
# the release's CHANGELOG: newlocale(0, ...) and the opaque, ownership-
# carrying pthread handle), so user/wolf-musl.patch retires and the tree
# is the tag's, unmodified; tools/mkwolf then stamps it as wolf-lang's
# own builder stamps a build at the tag (D57: WOLF_RELEASE=v0.2.35), so it
# says the release's line. No musl archive is published yet (#887).
# Until px65 (px60, at v0.2.34):
# tools/mkwolf built v0.2.34 plus wolf-musl.patch: newlocale(0,"C",NULL)
# instead of the unavailable LC_ALL_MASK binding, and an ownership wrapper
# making opaque pthread_t handles Send (musl uses a pointer-shaped handle).
# No libc source was read; newlocale(3) and pthread_join(3) specify the APIs.
# The patched tree carries a development stamp, never an unmodified-release
# stamp. Source revision plus patch digest identify its exact input.
# Move to a published archive once wolf-lang ships the fix and musl archive.
#
# Recipe: pinned Rust/musl target, cargo --release --locked, +crt-static,
# relocation-model=static (not the targets default static PIE), debug info
# and symbol tables stripped by rustc, linker build-id disabled,
# source/generated-target/registry paths remapped, three packages:
# wolf_driver, wolf_rt, wolf_cimport. No LLVM library: the LLVM backend emits
# IR and shells out to clang; the native backend embeds Cranelift. The helper
# installs nothing. The source/build directory is retained, never auto-deleted.
WOLF_SRC_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/wolf-lang
WOLF_SRC_TAG=v0.2.35
WOLF_SRC_REV=cf0c13d38479f444b69bb8356ad5709d07eff323
WOLF_SRC_TARGET=x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
WOLF_SRC_RUST=1.97.1
WOLF_SRC_PATCH=
WOLF_SRC_PATCH_SHA256=
WOLF_SRC_VERSION_LINE="wolf 0.2.35 (wolfgang, pin cf0c13d)"
WOLF_STD_REV=2386522eb059cca5a84108562c2c0a0e72345d34
